_096"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, 194","reason":"Writing a1=p and a2=q gives a7=5p+8q=120. Modulo 5, q=5t, so p=24-8t. The conditions 0<p<q force t=2, giving p=8 and q=10. Therefore a8=8p+13q=194.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1992_AMC_12_Q18","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"backward-recurrence-bounds","label":"Backward recurrence bounds","methodDirectNodeIds":{"backward-recurrence-bounds":["cnm_h200","cnm_099"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h200","cnm_099"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_h197","cnm_040","cnm_097"],"id":"backward-recurrence-and-bounds","label":"Work backward from the known term","methodDirectNodeIds":{"backward-recurrence-and-bounds":["cnm_h200","math:integer-diophantine-equations","cnm_099"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h200","math:integer-diophantine-equations","cnm_099","cnm_h197","cnm_040","cnm_097"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D. 64","reason":"Writing nickel, dime, and quarter counts as n, d, q gives d + 4q = 67 and n = 33 + 3q. Hence q ranges from 0 to 16, so d ranges from 67 to 3. The difference is 64.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2003_AMC_12B_Q07","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"eliminate-coin-counts","label":"Eliminate coin counts","methodDirectNodeIds":{"eliminate-coin-counts":["cnm_090","cnm_099"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_090","cnm_099"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, 8 coins","reason":"If there are N coins, the thickness bounds give 8 ≤ N ≤ 10. Multiplying thicknesses by 20 gives 31, 39, 27, and 35, each congruent to 3 modulo 4, while the total is 280. Thus 3N ≡ 0 modulo 4, so N is divisible by 4 and must be 8. Eight quarters attain the stated height.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonic